<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:v8">
<!--
    GH-8456: "ARM MRS (Banked register) instruction not implemented"
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/8456

    The ARMv7-A/v8 "MRS (Banked register)" form was missing from the decode
    table, so bytes 00 02 09 E1 (word 0xe1090200) failed to decode in ARM mode.
    Encoding: cond 00010 R 00 M1 Rd 001 M 0000 ; with R=0 it reads a banked GPR
    selected by SYSm = {M(bit8):M1(bits19:16)}.  Here R=0, M1=9, M=0 -> SYSm=9 =
    r9_fiq, so the instruction is "mrs r0,r9_fiq".

    Stage: S1 decode-table (SLEIGH spec-fix, no option).  The fix adds the
    MRS-banked constructors (R=0, both M halves) plus a banked-register name
    table.  This testcase pins the FIXED decode and forbids the bad/undefined
    rendering.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x0">
000209e1
</bytechunk>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>disassemble 0x0 0x4</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH8456 #1: MRS (Banked) decodes to 'mrs r0,r9_fiq'" min="1" max="1">^0x00000000: mrs[ ]+r0,r9_fiq</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH8456 #2: bytes no longer fail to decode" min="0" max="0">\?\?</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
